  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Integrated the pinned, Luksan-disabled NLopt closure as exact explicit-only nlopt-nelder-mead and nlopt-cobyla public methods. The implementation adds first-class scalar constraints, independently validates objective, bounds, feasibility, and local evidence, fails closed around unavailable or invalid resources, and preserves the ordinary-Python automatic route. Separate cminpack and NLopt adapter bundles are wired through Node, browser, relocated npm, Python SEA, production topology, capability, ABI, native-code, and Wasm inventories. The qualified source/artifact corpus, SciPy/PRIMA oracles, real Chromium, four supported hosts, public integration, resource-corruption, infeasibility, lifecycle, allocation, cancellation, and one-dimensional stopping regressions pass. Automatic selection remains disabled.",
    "risks": [
      "NLopt can return a positive termination code for an infeasible COBYLA point; the public integration deliberately recomputes and rejects such results independently.",
      "The full mathematical SEA was not rebuilt locally because this worktree lacks the optional native FLINT addon. Relocated sagepython SEA execution passes for both exact NLopt methods; repeat the full mathematical SEA in the native-prepared integration qualification.",
      "Optimizer-opportunity artifacts were intentionally not regenerated because the integration lane owns that shared dashboard.",
      "The browser cooperative receipt proves a pre-set shared-atomic force-stop; hard interruption of a non-returning callback is correctly provided by terminating and replacing its worker."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Merge the complete lane tip so both the qualified low-level backend and central public integration land together.",
      "Regenerate the optimizer-opportunity artifacts from the final integrated tree without enabling automatic NLopt selection.",
      "Repeat the full mathematical SEA qualification in a native-prepared checkout and retain the passing relocated sagepython SEA receipt."
    ]
  }
}
